  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} {S : Type u_2} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n  [inst_2 : CompleteSpace E] [inst_3 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [inst_4 : MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n  [inst_6 : MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : NNReal},\n  1 ≤ κ →\n    ContDiff ℝ 2 V →\n      (∀ (x v : E), (↑κ)⁻¹ * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x) v) v ∧ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x) v) v ≤ ‖v‖ ^ 2) →\n        ∀ {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E},\n          Measurable eta →\n            Measurable y →\n              (∀ (s : S), 0 < eta s) →\n                (∀ (s : S), eta s ≤ 1 / 2) →\n                  have F := fun s x => V x + (eta s)⁻¹ / 2 * ‖x - y s‖ ^ 2;\n                  ∃ p,\n                    Measurable p ∧\n                      (∀ (s : S), p s + eta s • gradient V (p s) = y s) ∧\n                        (∀ (s : S) (z : E),\n                            F s (p s) + ((↑κ)⁻¹ + (eta s)⁻¹) / 2 * ‖z - p s‖ ^ 2 ≤ F s z ∧\n                              (F s z ≤ F s (p s) ↔ z = p s)) ∧\n                          have G := fun q => gradient V (p q.1 + √(eta q.1) • q.2);\n                          Measurable G ∧\n                            ∃ K,\n                              ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel K ∧\n                                (∀ (s : S),\n                                    K s =\n                                      MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => G (s, z)) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)) ∧\n                                  ∀ (s : S),\n                                    MeasureTheory.MemLp (fun z => G (s, z)) 2 (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E) ∧\n                                      MeasureTheory.MemLp (fun z => G (s, z) - gradient V (p s)) 2\n                                          (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E) ∧\n                                        ∫ (z : E), ‖G (s, z) - gradient V (p s)‖ ^ 2 ∂ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E ≤\n                                            eta s * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) ∧\n                                          ∫ (z : E), ‖G (s, z)‖ ^ 2 ∂ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E ≤\n                                              2 * ‖gradient V (p s)‖ ^ 2 + 2 * eta s * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) ∧\n                                            MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun w => ‖w‖ ^ 2) (K s) ∧\n                                              ∫ (w : E), ‖w‖ ^ 2 ∂K s ≤\n                                                2 * ‖gradient V (p s)‖ ^ 2 + 2 * eta s * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E)",
    "statement_sha256": "e95a13401a10cc527d5c5bc2350715d08fbf3f0d2cc64088e4947942510f9018",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "NNReal is the type of nonnegative real numbers,with its displayed coercion into the real numbers. Module.finrank is the finite real vector-space dimension. ContDiff R 2 means twice continuously Frechet differentiable. fderiv is the Frechet derivative and gradient is the genuine real inner-product gradient. Scalar multiplication,real inverse and square root retain their displayed Lean definitions.",
      "ProbabilityTheory.Kernel is a measurable measure-valued transition interface; IsMarkovKernel asserts that every fiber is a probability measure. Measure.map denotes pushforward. stdGaussian is the standard centered Gaussian with identity covariance on the displayed finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space.",
      "MeasureTheory.MemLp f 2 mu asserts almost-everywhere strong measurability and finite L2 seminorm of f under mu. Integrable f mu means Bochner integrability. Displayed real integrals are Bochner integrals; their total Lean definition alone does not assert integrability. Product inputs and all existential/universal quantifiers retain their displayed order. No extra topology or measure is supplied on a parameter space unless shown."
    ]
